{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/829758-how-to-keep-heros-alive","id":829758,"title":":How to keep Heros alive?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-14T09:13:06-08:00","id":829758,"title":":How to keep Heros alive?","content":"Ideas on how to keep a hero alive as a long term antaganist I dont want to depend entirely on the Broods sense of Mercy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T09:40:51-08:00","id":829765,"title":"","content":"Have the Hero ingratiate himself with local and regional authorities. Fling mud at the Brood's reputation. Gather henchmen and cronies. Arrange fights so that it looks like it was the Brood that came asking for trouble.<br /> <br /> Make deals with other types of supernaturals, especially Mages. Team up with Hunters and other Heroes for as long as possible.<br /> <br /> Don't be afraid to come up with new Gifts for an unusual Hero. A professional outdoorsman and big game hunter might have a Gift that lets him bypass supernatural senses, which would force Beasts to rely on their unmodified Perception dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T09:44:23-08:00","id":829768,"title":"","content":"yes Im wanting to keep him alive in DEFEAT if that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T09:51:35-08:00","id":829771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/829758-how-to-keep-heros-alive?p=829768#post829768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes Im wanting to keep him alive in DEFEAT if that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could have the Brood gather as many allies and contacts as possible to gather evidence of the Hero's criminal activities. A sort of tug of war where each side is trying to expose the dirt under the fingernails of the other, at the risk of getting caught using the same methods. If the Brood wins, the Hero is arrested and is hopefully devastated enough to give up on Heroism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T09:58:54-08:00","id":829774,"title":"","content":"Short Answer: don't take the party on in a straight fight. Use proxies, indirect attacks, and the element of surprise to build up tension. Make the party learn who's out to get them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T10:14:10-08:00","id":829784,"title":"","content":"If I read you correctly, you're looking for an exit strategy for the Hero to take on the Beasts in direct confrontation (likely in the Lair) and still get away? What kind of thematic underpinning do you have in mind for the Hero in question? Are they foolhardy and failed each time, resolute and trusting in the universe to spare them, nihilistic, a cartoon villain?<br /> <br /> I've got a few suggestions, just checking to make sure I'm mentally on point. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2320-tilting-clock","name":"Tilting Clock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T10:16:16-08:00","id":829787,"title":"","content":"Make the Hero the cowardly type, you know first to bail when the situation gets bad. I mean I have made great use staggered flashbangs.* <br /> <br /> Having the Hero be a subordinate might help. I mean different supernaturals would have different ways of protecting their pet Hero, or hell have some tyrant spawned centuries old Hero pulling the strings with part of his trick literally being that he still gets a boost from his subordinates killing a Beast.<br /> <br /> *Granted not so helpful if one of the pcs has the blinding light lair trait, but it is probably not good to have someone you want living for a while to fight the group with no knowledge anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T14:04:37-08:00","id":829866,"title":"","content":"the hero im thinking up right now is a frat boy whos just grabbed a Weapon for the first time and begin hunting monsters. The games mostly vampire but I decided to allow a si ngle beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T19:19:24-08:00","id":829979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/829758-how-to-keep-heros-alive?p=829866#post829866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the hero im thinking up right now is a frat boy whos just grabbed a Weapon for the first time and begin hunting monsters. The games mostly vampire but I decided to allow a si ngle beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm well if he's basically been a hero less than a week I wouldn't expect him to survive to be honest. <br /> <br /> Stacking the deck in favor of the hero I would say have him as part of a group. More people makes it harder for a Beast to escape, justifies the hero bringing them, and when things go south they could drag the hero off. <br /> <br /> You'll also want this to be in a fairly public area. From the hero's perspective this means more witnesses to see their triumph over the Beast. From the ST position it might limit the Beast's attack options depending on how willing the Beast is to draw attention to themselves and if the vampires are present masquerade rules will probably inhibit them from breaking out the big powers. Plus I mean getting attacked isn't that much of a problem for the group to handle. Even without supernatural abilities the cops show up ask what happened you go, &quot;I don't know freaking nut job came up howling crap about monsters and started shooting at people.&quot; Now granted they can justify killing the dude who just came in and tried to kill them, but there are fewer methods available to do the killing and the cops will be asking far more questions since people died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T19:54:06-08:00","id":829992,"title":"","content":"Make the Hero a family member. Not &quot;Family&quot; family, but a sibling, parent or child from before the Beast's Homecoming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}